 \"--\" must not cause an error or change the exit code.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Flag behavior\n    items:\n      - R2.1: --help must print a usage summary to stdout and exit with code 0. The usage text must include the utility name and a brief description of its purpose.\n      - R2.2: --version must print a version string to stdout and exit with code 0. The version string is set at build time via -ldflags; it defaults to \"dev\" when unset.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Signal handling\n    items:\n      - R3.1: |\n          Must not exit non-zero due to SIGPIPE when stdout is closed by a downstream\n          consumer. At startup, install a SIGPIPE handler: use signal.Notify(c,\n          syscall.SIGPIPE) with a buffered channel of size 1; in a dedicated goroutine\n          call os.Exit(0) when the channel receives. Do not use signal.Ignore.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes\n    items:\n      - R4.1: Must exit 0 in all cases — normal operation, --help, --version, and SIGPIPE.\n      - R4.2: Must exit 0 even when unknown arguments are passed (true never fails).\n\n  R5:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R5.1: The reference binary for differential testing is gtrue (Homebrew GNU coreutils).\n      - R5.2: Differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/true does not implement any I/O operations beyond flag output (--help, --version).\n  - cmd/true does not implement short flags (-h, -v) for help and version; only GNU long flags (--help, --version) are supported, matching gtrue behavior.\n  - cmd/true does not validate or interpret non-flag arguments.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: go run ./cmd/true exits with code 0 and produces no stdout or stderr output.\"\n  - \"AC2: go run ./cmd/true --help prints usage to stdout and exits 0, matching gtrue --help output structure.\"\n  - \"AC3: go run ./cmd/true --version prints a version string to stdout and exits 0.\"\n  - \"AC4: go run ./cmd/true with arbitrary non-flag arguments (e.g., true foo bar) exits with code 0.\"\n  - \"AC5: Differential test against gtrue passes for no-args, --help, and --version modes.\"\n  - \"AC6: cmd/true compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Rd1ZgFPKEaTsghGKJH4DDp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MAiy4kjT6oHM7HLBEXkmWu","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/254/docs/specs/product-requirements/prd013-false.yaml","content":"id: prd013-false\ntitle: \"cmd/false: Exit Unsuccessfully\"\n\nproblem: |\n  The false utility is the complement of true: it does nothing and exits with code 1.\n  Despite its simplicity, a formal specification is needed to ensure the Go\n  implementation matches GNU coreutils false exactly — including --help and --version\n  flag behavior (which exit 0, not 1), exit codes for each case, and SIGPIPE handling.\n  The reference binary for differential testing is gfalse (Homebrew GNU coreutils with\n  g- prefix). Without a specification, the --help and --version exit code behavior\n  (exit 0, overriding the default exit 1) can be missed.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Exit with code 1 unconditionally in normal operation (no flags).\n  - G2: Support --help flag that prints usage information to stdout and exits 0.\n  - G3: Support --version flag that prints version string to stdout and exits 0.\n  - G4: Handle SIGPIPE cleanly by exiting without error.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior (no flags, no arguments)\n    items:\n      - R1.1: Must exit with code 1 when invoked with no arguments.\n      - R1.2: Must produce no output on stdout in normal operation (no flags).\n      - R1.3: Must produce no output on stderr in normal operation (no flags).\n      - R1.4: Must not read from stdin. Stdin must be left untouched.\n      - R1.5: Must ignore any non-flag arguments passed on the command line. Arguments that do not start with \"--\" must not cause an error or change the exit code from 1.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Flag behavior\n    items:\n      - R2.1: --help must print a usage summary to stdout and exit with code 0. The usage text must include the utility name and a brief description of its purpose. Note that --help overrides the default exit code of 1.\n      - R2.2: --version must print a version string to stdout and exit with code 0. The version string is set at build time via -ldflags; it defaults to \"dev\" when unset. Note that --version overrides the default exit code of 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Signal handling\n    items:\n      - R3.1: |\n          Must not exit non-zero due to SIGPIPE when stdout is closed by a downstream\n          consumer. At startup, install a SIGPIPE handler: use signal.Notify(c,\n          syscall.SIGPIPE) with a buffered channel of size 1; in a dedicated goroutine\n          call os.Exit(0) when the channel receives. Do not use signal.Ignore.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes\n    items:\n      - R4.1: Must exit 1 in normal operation (no flags) and when unknown arguments are passed.\n      - R4.2: Must exit 0 when --help is given.\n      - R4.3: Must exit 0 when --version is given.\n      - R4.4: Must exit 0 on SIGPIPE (matching the SIGPIPE handler behavior).\n\n  R5:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R5.1: The reference binary for differential testing is gfalse (Homebrew GNU coreutils).\n      - R5.2: Differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/false does not implement any I/O operations beyond flag output (--help, --version).\n  - cmd/false does not implement short flags (-h, -v) for help and version; only GNU long flags (--help, --version) are supported, matching gfalse behavior.\n  - cmd/false does not validate or interpret non-flag arguments.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: go run ./cmd/false exits with code 1 and produces no stdout or stderr output.\"\n  - \"AC2: go run ./cmd/false --help prints usage to stdout and exits 0, matching gfalse --help output structure.\"\n  - \"AC3: go run ./cmd/false --version prints a version string to stdout and exits 0.\"\n  - \"AC4: go run ./cmd/false with arbitrary non-flag arguments (e.g., false foo bar) exits with code 1.\"\n  - \"AC5: Differential test against gfalse passes for no-args, --help, and --version modes.\"\n  - \"AC6: cmd/false compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":118625,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d60d98e-2c55-476a-91fa-87a9ea5b4b77","uuid":"fd53635f-7221-4828-857a-d3ce7d27cf6f"}
